Okay, here is a list of the characters I have experience with and a rating
(1-5, 5 is easiest) for each one.

Barbarian: A good choice for hack and slash tactics.  He is tough enough to
           handle most encounters withouth thinking, and his poison resistance
           makes life easier.

Rating: 4


Valkyrie: Probably the best choice if you want to play a chaotic character.
          Although they lack poison resistance, they start with a longsword,
          which after becoming Excalibur makes minced meat for your foes.

Rating: 5


Healer:   Well, what can I say?  I just had to win with a healer, and I did.
          It was far from easy; they start with nothing useful save 8 potions
          which were essential.  I blessed the extra healing potions and got
          20 extra hit points, and the healing potions were saved for holy
          water.  The wand of sleep he starts with gets well used.

Rating: 1


Wizard:   See some of my comments in my previous article (Can wizards survive?)
          I find them quite playable, but not as easy as a valkyrie because
          they require constant thinking until late in the game.

Rating: 4


Archaeologist:
          Not too bad, but far from good.  I don't believe the spoiler file
          when it mentions his "tinning kit (vital)"  It is a heavy luxury
          item which is pretty useless.  Being stealthy and fast help him
          survive, but his ability to identify gems on sight is no big deal.
          This is just a luxury (a REEEEEL nice one, I admit) which does
          nothing to help him survive except save his identify scrolls for
          better uses.  (which we all of course do anyway) :-)

Rating: 2


Tourist:  Another one I tried for kicks...  Like the spoiler file says, I
          had fun with this guy.  He starts with some good tools and lots
          of money and food, making the early game pretty easy.  From there,
          it gets much tougher but not at all impossible.

Rating: 3


Samurai:  Similar to the Barbarian, but Lawful.  He doesn't have poison
          resistance, but his kicking ability and speed make up for that.

Rating: 4


Those are all the characters I have real experience with.  Out of the others,
a Priest is supposed to be pretty good because of his ability to detect the
cursed/uncursd/blessed state of objects he finds.  He can also kick well, but
I haven't ever won with one; I don't find his special ability to be that useful
since there are several other methods to determine an object's cursed/blessed
state, but I am apparently in the minority opinion on that point.
